  "implementation": [
    "Borrow::pin_job compares exact shared prepared State and pins the stable shared JobState with a noncopyable/nonmovable JobScope, checking actual child identity/PTD. JobMemory logical return atomically refuses nonzero pin count.",
    "SessionMemoryDomain::enter(job) owns stable heap scope independently of movable token address; Parent publishes active scope only after full admission. Constructor failure releases provisional pin. Default enter retains original-worker-only behavior.",
    "Source effects validate active scope/exact backing/PTD. Operation exit validates permission/PTD, clears published pointer/activity before scope release while Parent gate remains held. Parent->root lock order is consistent; no root callback into Parent.",
    "Parent prepare_job uses existing whole normal Operation and original Borrow worker. Parent reap_jobs uses existing mutation reservation across unlocked OS polling; close/enter/lease cannot retire underlying Borrow mid-call. Unknown outcomes poison.",
    "Parent.close checks logical child completion/no pins before owner/lifecycle movement. Pending jobs leave open Parent and all owners intact. Post-retirement catch/postcheck cannot overwrite poisoned prefix with Closed.",
    "Job-scope loss/token abandonment retains root and row, rejects later source effects and poisons Parent. Source closure remains logical Borrow return; actual original+child OS/FLS exit is still required by PreparedMemory.close before backing release."
  ],
